course: dictionary
lesson: 3705
title: A fleck of something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fleck is a tiny spot or a very small piece of something. It can be a colour, like a fleck of paint, or a bit of dust or mud. «Space junk is broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth very fast, and even a small fleck of paint can damage a spacecraft.» Here, a fleck is so small you might barely see it, but it still matters.
explain: Fleck can also be a verb. To be flecked with something means to have tiny spots of it scattered over you or over a surface. «Her green eyes were flecked with gold.» Her eyes are not all gold. Only small spots of gold are scattered through the green.
explain: Look at the words around fleck to check its meaning. Words like «of», «with» and «flecks of» often tell you that a fleck is a small amount of something. Ask yourself: is the writer describing something tiny and scattered? If yes, fleck is probably a spot or a small piece.
fact: A fleck is a tiny spot or mark of colour, or a small piece of something.
fact: «Flecks of» means small amounts scattered here and there, like «flecks of gold» in a green eye.
fact: As a verb, «flecked with» means having small spots of something scattered over it.
fact: «Fleck» can be a noun or a verb: «a fleck of mud» is a noun, and «the sky was flecked with clouds» uses it as a verb.
fact: In space, even a fleck of paint can be dangerous, because space junk moves very fast.
exercise: «Her green eyes had flecks of gold in them.» What are the flecks of gold? | A gold ring | Gold paint in a tin | Big gold coins | *Tiny spots of gold
exercise: «The old wall was flecked with white paint.» What does flecked mean here? | Was made completely white | *Had small spots of white paint scattered over it | Was cleaned and polished | Was blown away by the wind
exercise: «Even a fleck of paint can damage a spacecraft.» Why is a tiny fleck of paint a problem in space? | *Because it can travel very fast and hit a spacecraft | Because it sticks to the Earth | Because space is too cold for paint | Because paint is very heavy
test: «There was a fleck of mud on his shoe.» What is a fleck in this sentence? | A hole in the ground | A large puddle | *A tiny spot or small piece | A loud noise
test: «The night sky was flecked with stars.» What does flecked mean? | Covered with dark clouds | Blown away by the wind | Made completely dark | *Had small bright spots scattered over it
exam: «Space junk is broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth very fast, and space agencies track it.» Why do space agencies track space junk, even when it is only a fleck of paint? | Because it is pretty to look at | Because it is worth a lot of money | *Because even a tiny fleck can damage a spacecraft | Because it makes the sky brighter
